### 1. Disable Delegates in `DynamicInputSliceOpModel` in `tensorflow/lite/kernels/slice_test.cc`

#### Issue
When tests are executed with delegates enabled (e.g. combined delegate test suites), delegates can intercept the op and alter the output tensor allocation type (`kTfLiteArenaRw` instead of `kTfLiteDynamic`) or error behavior. To ensure `DynamicInputSliceOpModel` directly tests the built-in CPU SLICE kernel's dynamic allocation and error handling, delegates should be bypassed for this model.

#### Fix
Update the `BuildInterpreter` invocation in `DynamicInputSliceOpModel` in `tensorflow/lite/kernels/slice_test.cc` to pass `/*apply_delegate=*/false`:

```diff
diff --git a/tensorflow/lite/kernels/slice_test.cc b/tensorflow/lite/kernels/slice_test.cc
--- a/tensorflow/lite/kernels/slice_test.cc
+++ b/tensorflow/lite/kernels/slice_test.cc
@@ -120,7 +120,9 @@ class DynamicInputSliceOpModel : public SingleOpModel {
     output_ = AddOutput(output_data);
     SetBuiltinOp(BuiltinOperator_SLICE, BuiltinOptions_SliceOptions,
                  CreateSliceOptions(builder_).Union());
-    BuildInterpreter({input_data.shape, begin_shape, size_shape});
+    BuildInterpreter({input_data.shape, begin_shape, size_shape},
+                     /*num_threads=*/-1, /*allow_fp32_relax_to_fp16=*/false,
+                     /*apply_delegate=*/false);
   }

   void SetInput(std::initializer_list<float> data) {
```

