The presubmit tests failed on GPU for `//tensorflow/python/kernel_tests/nn_ops:pooling_ops_test_gpu` with the following error:

```
InvalidArgumentError: {{function_node __wrapped__AvgPoolGrad_device_/job:localhost/replica:0/task:0/device:GPU:0}} Pooling would produce zero-sized spatial output. input: 2x1 window: 1x2 stride: 1x1 [Op:AvgPoolGrad]
```

### Root Cause

In `tensorflow/core/kernels/pooling_ops_common.cc`, `RequirePositiveSpatialOutput(context, params)` was added unconditionally to `DnnPoolingImpl`. Because `DnnPoolingImpl` is shared by both `MaxPool` (`kMaximum`) and `AvgPool` (`kAverage`) on GPU, this causes forward and gradient average pooling operations with zero-sized spatial dimensions (such as in `testAvgPoolGradOutputWithZeroDim`) to fail with `InvalidArgumentError` instead of returning the expected zeroed output tensor.

Additionally, `tensorflow/core/kernels/mkl/mkl_avgpooling_op.cc` had an unintended check added for average pooling.

### Required Fix

1. In `tensorflow/core/kernels/pooling_ops_common.cc`, update `DnnPoolingImpl` to only enforce `RequirePositiveSpatialOutput` when `pooling_mode == se::dnn::PoolingMode::kMaximum`, and retain the early-return check `if (params.out_height == 0 || params.out_width == 0) return;` for other pooling modes:

```diff
--- a/tensorflow/core/kernels/pooling_ops_common.cc
+++ b/tensorflow/core/kernels/pooling_ops_common.cc
@@ -250,9 +250,15 @@ void DnnPoolingImpl(OpKernelContext* context, se::dnn::PoolingMode pooling_mode,
   if (!context->status().ok()) {
     return;
   }

-  // Forward cudnn pooling only (grads use DnnPoolingGradImpl).
-  RequirePositiveSpatialOutput(context, params);
-  if (!context->status().ok()) {
+  // Forward MaxPool only: oversized VALID windows must raise InvalidArgument.
+  if (pooling_mode == se::dnn::PoolingMode::kMaximum) {
+    RequirePositiveSpatialOutput(context, params);
+    if (!context->status().ok()) {
+      return;
+    }
+  }
+
+  if (params.out_height == 0 || params.out_width == 0) {
     return;
   }
```

2. In `tensorflow/core/kernels/mkl/mkl_avgpooling_op.cc`, remove the `OP_REQUIRES` check for `pool_params.out_height > 0 && pool_params.out_width > 0` so that `MklAvgPoolingOp` behavior is not affected.

