### 2. Masking Pole Inputs in `packetOp`

In `tensorflow/core/kernels/cwise_ops.h`, `digamma_op::packetOp` directly evaluates `Eigen::internal::scalar_digamma_op<Scalar>().packetOp(x)` before selecting out the poles:

```cpp
    Packet infs = pset1<Packet>(-Eigen::NumTraits<Scalar>::infinity());
    Packet nans = pset1<Packet>(Eigen::NumTraits<Scalar>::quiet_NaN());
    Packet digamma_x = Eigen::internal::scalar_digamma_op<Scalar>().packetOp(x);

    Packet result = pselect(is_negative_integer, nans, digamma_x);
    return pselect(is_zero, infs, result);
```

When vector lanes in `x` contain `0.0` or negative integers, evaluating `packetOp(x)` unconditionally can trigger division-by-zero or undefined floating-point exceptions in SIMD registers before `pselect` executes. 

Please mask out pole values with a safe non-pole dummy value (e.g. `1.0`) before evaluating `packetOp`:

```cpp
  template <typename Packet>
  EIGEN_DEVICE_FUNC EIGEN_STRONG_INLINE Packet packetOp(const Packet& x) const {
    Packet zeros = pzero(x);
    Packet is_zero = pcmp_eq(x, zeros);
    Packet is_lt_zero = pcmp_lt(x, zeros);
    Packet is_integer = pcmp_eq(x, pfloor(x));
    Packet is_negative_integer = pand(is_lt_zero, is_integer);
    Packet is_pole = por(is_zero, is_negative_integer);

    // Replace pole inputs with a safe non-pole value (1.0) before computing digamma.
    Packet safe_x = pselect(is_pole, pset1<Packet>(Scalar(1.)), x);

    Packet infs = pset1<Packet>(-Eigen::NumTraits<Scalar>::infinity());
    Packet nans = pset1<Packet>(Eigen::NumTraits<Scalar>::quiet_NaN());
    Packet digamma_x = Eigen::internal::scalar_digamma_op<Scalar>().packetOp(safe_x);

    Packet result = pselect(is_negative_integer, nans, digamma_x);
    return pselect(is_zero, infs, result);
  }
```

### 1. Fix Incorrect Metadata Protobuf Field Setter in `Init()`

In `tensorflow/core/util/debug_events_writer.cc`, `metadata->set_tensorflow_version(...)` is called twice instead of setting `metadata->set_file_version(...)`. The second call overwrites `tensorflow_version` with the format version string and leaves `file_version` unset.

```diff
   DebugEvent debug_event;
   DebugMetadata* metadata = debug_event.mutable_debug_metadata();
   metadata->set_tensorflow_version(TF_VERSION_STRING);
-  metadata->set_tensorflow_version(
+  metadata->set_file_version(
