### Summary
The build fails across CI checks ([Linux CPU](https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/actions/runs/33179790804/job/98878842911), [Linux CUDA](https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/actions/runs/33179790804/job/98878843211), [ARM64](https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/actions/runs/33179790804/job/98878843218), [Windows](https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/actions/runs/33179790804/job/98878843108)) due to a C++ compilation error in `tensorflow/core/common_runtime/eager/validate_function_devices.cc`.

### Root Cause
In `tensorflow/core/common_runtime/eager/validate_function_devices.cc` line 64, `absl::StrEqualsIgnoreCase` is called, but the Abseil function declared in `absl/strings/match.h` is `absl::EqualsIgnoreCase`:

```text
tensorflow/core/common_runtime/eager/validate_function_devices.cc:64:17: error: no member named 'StrEqualsIgnoreCase' in namespace 'absl'; did you mean 'EqualsIgnoreCase'?
      if (absl::StrEqualsIgnoreCase(parsed_device.type, avail_type.type_string())) {
                ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
                EqualsIgnoreCase
```

### Required Fix
Update `absl::StrEqualsIgnoreCase` to `absl::EqualsIgnoreCase`:

```diff
diff --git a/tensorflow/core/common_runtime/eager/validate_function_devices.cc b/tensorflow/core/common_runtime/eager/validate_function_devices.cc
--- a/tensorflow/core/common_runtime/eager/validate_function_devices.cc
+++ b/tensorflow/core/common_runtime/eager/validate_function_devices.cc
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ absl::Status ValidateFunctionDeviceConstraints(
     // Check if the requested device type is available.
     bool device_type_available = false;
     for (const DeviceType& avail_type : supported_device_types) {
-      if (absl::StrEqualsIgnoreCase(parsed_device.type, avail_type.type_string())) {
+      if (absl::EqualsIgnoreCase(parsed_device.type, avail_type.type_string())) {
         device_type_available = true;
         break;
       }
```
